## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) parity of `components/ai/AISuggestNewGeofences.tsx` at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AISuggestNewGeofences.*` — **9 files, ~2,290 lines**, following the established sibling-surface pattern (`AIAutoNameUnnamedLocations`) exactly:

- **Adapter** (pure logic): nested `draft_geofence` tool_result decode, stream/connection/gate enums, button logic, accessibility summary.
- **Model** (P1/S8): `SuggestGeofenceSource` seam, `@Observable` model, `view.opened` telemetry (P1/S11), in-memory source, P1/S10 i18n facade.
- **View / Views / Chrome**: gate switch, freshness chip+banner, header, Helix badge, action button, proposal box (name + rounded radius), output panel, gate loading/error chrome.
- **Previews / strings / Tests / ModelTests**: every state + full coverage.

I used per-surface uniquely-named types (`SuggestGeofence*`) since `AIJSONValue`/`GeofenceDraft` are already owned elsewhere.

